{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7b89f8134e7e286bb055f5770d1c904284ab82dd4a49a6d130e5c37c8eb68144","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review trigger framework / project overlays","key_entities":[".rebar/criteria_routing.json","code_review.concurrency","content_triggered_overlays","docs/llm-framework.md","tests/unit/test_code_review_triggers.py","trigger_tokens","applies_to",".lock","retry","Popen","setsid","fork","stage_and_commit","push_tickets_branch","refs/reconciler/"],"problem_keywords":["trigger vocabulary","concurrency detection","project overlay","two-layer trigger design","fire-rate tradeoff","code review routing"],"propositions":["The rebar project requires a project-layer trigger overlay entry to detect concurrency-related changes (lock files, retry logic, subprocess operations) that the committed high-precision tier misses.","The committed tier triggers on 13.3% of diffs while adding the project noisy tier increases fire rate by 22.0%, and three corpus bugs only trigger via project-layer tokens like .lock.","The two-layer trigger design (committed high-precision vs. project-specific vocabulary) lacks documentation, preventing other projects from adopting the pattern.","A config-effect test must verify that a diff containing index.lock fires the concurrency overlay under this repo's effective routing but not under committed-only routing."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787892281500479001,"uuid":"c57c0647-3d87-4263-a273-6e4185395b58"}